  "description": "Application for a Non-Material Amendment Following a Grant of Planning Permission ref: 22/02489/FUL (Demolition of 99-101 Waterloo Road, 103-107 Waterloo Road, 124 and 126 Cornwall Road and redevelopment comprising a new 20 storey office building (Class E (g)) and flexible ancillary uses (Class E (a), (b)) together with the refurbishment of 109-119 Waterloo Road ('Mercury House') for flexible Class E to a specified area, and Class E (a), (b), (g) and Sui Generis (bar) uses to specified areas, and basement excavation, works to the public highway, public realm, new landscaping, ancillary and enabling works, plant and equipment) granted on 04.06.2024.\r\rAmendment sought :\r-To introduce a new condition 101 to allow the scheme to be carried out in four phases:\rPhase 0: Enabling works;\rPhase 1: Demolition works;\rPhase 2: Construction of Mercury House;\rPhase 3: Construction of Waterloo Central Tower.\r\r- Revise wording to conditions: \rCondition 4: Method Statement and Building Condition Report (Commemorative Plaques);\rCondition 6: Air Quality and Dust Management Plan (AQDMP);\rCondition 7: Land Contamination;\rCondition 8: Basement Impact Assessment (BIA);\rCondition 9: Method of Demolition Statement;\rCondition 10: Construction and Environmental Management Plan (CEMP);\rCondition 11: Construction Logistics Plan (CLP);\rCondition 14: Sustainable Drainage System (SuDS) Strategy;\rCondition 73: Air Source Heat Pumps;\rCondition 77: Bird and Bat Boxes;\rCondition 83: Hard and Soft Landscaping Scheme;\rCondition 91: Threat and Vulnerability Risk Assessment;\rCondition 92: Structural Blast Survey;\rCondition 98: Full Fibre Connectivity Infrastructure;\rCondition 100: Acoustic Feasibility and Design.",
